{
  "about": "The library rule (docs/dev/work_folders.md \"The library rule\"): which root pages the library lists and which are library documents. A page's properties in; listed (the library lists it: no work_folder, or library true), in_listing (the listing route carries it: listed, or pinned with a non-empty string), library_document (a paper: a work folder's file only when library is true; any other page unless its document is read in place) and library_pdf (a library document whose document is a PDF it owns) out. work_folder is a non-empty string or none; library is true or absent, and only true counts. Read by backend/tests/test_work_folders_library.py (gamma/work_folders/library.py, and the same answers from SQL_LISTED, SQL_IN_LISTING and doc_id IS NOT NULL AND SQL_LIBRARY_PDF over the page as a root row) and frontend/tests/library.test.mjs (frontend/src/documents/library.js).",
